/target
.env
*.pdb

# Machine-specific: the MCP server is launched by absolute path, and a committed
# entry pointing at a binary that does not exist on the cloner's disk throws an
# error in their client every session. Copy .mcp.json.example instead.
.mcp.json

# Same reasoning: this project's Claude Code config is user-scope only, so the
# server and its hooks are registered once in ~/.claude and never here. Accepting
# a permission prompt writes .claude/settings.json back anyway, and a committed
# copy would apply one machine's answers to everyone who clones.
/.claude/
